<title>GERMANY: Pan-German July adj numbers in work rise mth/mth.</title>
<headline>Pan-German July adj numbers in work rise mth/mth.</headline>
<dateline>WIESBADEN, Germany 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Statistics Office reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p> PAN-GERMAN NUMBERS IN WORK		Jul 96     Jun 96     Jul 95</p>
<p> Number in work (1)(unadj, million)    34.441     34.511     34.742</p>
<p> Number in work (1)(seas adj, million) 34.548     34.538     34.852</p>
<p> Number in work (2)(seas adj, million) 34.589     34.580     34.894</p>
<p>WEST GERMAN</p>
<p> Number in work (unadj,million)	  28.161     28.252     28.427</p>
<p> Number in work (seas adj, million)    28.245     28.245     28.513</p>
<p>EAST GERMAN</p>
<p> Number in work (unadj, million)	  6.337	6.322	6.374</p>
<p> Number in work (seas adj, million)     6.344	6.335	6.381</p>
<p>NOTE - Pan-German figure marked (1) refer to people living in Germany. Those marked (2), as well as all the west and east German figures, refer to people working in the respective regions but not necessarily living in Germany.</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-2609750</p>
</text>
